		},
		{
			"id": "t-89",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 56,
			"y": 1567.6,
			"width": 876.5859375,
			"height": 252,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [
				"g-86"
			],
			"frameId": null,
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1083438815,
			"version": 2,
			"versionNonce": 1939280135,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1795545616549,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1. client.query(query, dry_run=True)  → dry\n2. dry.statement_type == 'SELECT'    else [{ error: 'Only a single SELECT statement is allowed.' }]\n3. referenced tables within allowed_tables()    (the 15 current_* views plus the tables they read; built\nonce by dry-running SELECT * on each view)\n   else [{ error: 'Only these views may be queried: [...]' }]\n4. log.append(query)                  → answer.queries\n5. client.query(query, maximum_bytes_billed = 1_000_000_000)\n   job.result(max_results = 200)      (1 GB cap; over it → BadRequest → [{ error }])\n6. run.bytes_billed = job.total_bytes_billed;   json_rows(rows) makes them JSON-safe\n\nEvery view reads precomputed counters, so a typical question bills kilobytes.\nViews: current_champion_stats, _trait_stats, _item_stats, _champion_item_stats / _pair_ / _trio_,\n_composition_stats, _composition_variant_stats, _composition_star_upgrade_stats,\n_composition_completed_item_stats, _composition_board_cost_stats, _composition_unit_stats,\n_composition_trait_stats, _matches, _participant_compositions",
			"originalText": "1. client.query(query, dry_run=True)  → dry\n2. dry.statement_type == 'SELECT'    else [{ error: 'Only a single SELECT statement is allowed.' }]\n3. referenced tables within allowed_tables()    (the 15 current_* views plus the tables they read; built\nonce by dry-running SELECT * on each view)\n   else [{ error: 'Only these views may be queried: [...]' }]\n4. log.append(query)                  → answer.queries\n5. client.query(query, maximum_bytes_billed = 1_000_000_000)\n   job.result(max_results = 200)      (1 GB cap; over it → BadRequest → [{ error }])\n6. run.bytes_billed = job.total_bytes_billed;   json_rows(rows) makes them JSON-safe\n\nEvery view reads precomputed counters, so a typical question bills kilobytes.\nViews: current_champion_stats, _trait_stats, _item_stats, _champion_item_stats / _pair_ / _trio_,\n_composition_stats, _composition_variant_stats, _composition_star_upgrade_stats,\n_composition_completed_item_stats, _composition_board_cost_stats, _composition_unit_stats,\n_composition_trait_stats, _matches, _participant_compositions",
			"fontSize": 14,
			"fontFamily": 3,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"lineHeight": 1.2,
			"autoResize": true,
			"index": "b0E",
