			"updated": 1795545616549,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "full = {\n  level: 8,\n  units:    [{ name, cost, copies, copies_out }],\n  tier_out: [{ cost, copies }],\n  results:  [{ gold: 80, rolls: 12, all_units: 0.7312, per_unit: { Lillia: 0.81 } }, ...],   // one row \n  per asked gold\n  curve:    [{ gold, rolls, all_units, per_unit }, ...]    // one point per Roll, from the gold that \n  buys the copies, until >= 95 %\n}\nanswer.roll_odds.append(full)              → HTTP body → RollOddsChart\nresult = { k: v for k, v in full if k != 'curve' }       → Gemini (keeps its context small)\nanswer.roll_odds_runs += RollOddsRun{ args, latency_ms, error }     (inputs only, never the odds)\nerror → { error: str(exc) } so Gemini can retry (unknown unit lists the valid names)",
			"originalText": "full = {\n  level: 8,\n  units:    [{ name, cost, copies, copies_out }],\n  tier_out: [{ cost, copies }],\n  results:  [{ gold: 80, rolls: 12, all_units: 0.7312, per_unit: { Lillia: 0.81 } }, ...],   // one row \n  per asked gold\n  curve:    [{ gold, rolls, all_units, per_unit }, ...]    // one point per Roll, from the gold that \n  buys the copies, until >= 95 %\n}\nanswer.roll_odds.append(full)              → HTTP body → RollOddsChart\nresult = { k: v for k, v in full if k != 'curve' }       → Gemini (keeps its context small)\nanswer.roll_odds_runs += RollOddsRun{ args, latency_ms, error }     (inputs only, never the odds)\nerror → { error: str(exc) } so Gemini can retry (unknown unit lists the valid names)",
